                    "message": "Thank you very much for the feedback. I will think of your suggestions in future patches and fix this for this patch in follow-ups."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/systems_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 125,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "&&\n\nAll temporary functions should be passed by move."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/systems_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 125,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/systems_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 128,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "We generally wouldn't hardcode EntityManager specifically.  We'd request the mapper.\n\nIt might be ok in this case?  what do you think?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/systems_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 128,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "I hardcoded the service in order to move from a getSubTree call to a getSubTreePaths call, which performs a little bit faster. \n\nI assumed it will be ok, since the ManagedHost interface primarly targets multi-host systems, with the only one using the interface being yv4 from which I now configures via EM. From my understanding I got skimming through older discord discussions, PIM is seen more as the legacy inventory manager, newer machines would configure via EM."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/systems_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 167,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This function returns an iterator.  Technically this is taking a reference to an rvalue.  Clearly this works for you so it must not be a problem"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/systems_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 180,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Is this required?  Could we just do *found on the next line?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/systems_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 223,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Would've like to see the object_path string builder routines used here instead of std::string, but this isn't an actual vulnerability because computerSystemIndex will always be a valid path.\n\nAll gooe, just thoughts for the future."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/include/utils/systems_utils.hpp",
                    "line": 223,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "I did try to use the / operator from object_path to append the index with object_path routines, but it fails to convert from uint64_t (unless we call to_string on it first, but that leaves us with the same problem)."
                }
            ],
